<title>AUSTRIA: Bank Austria denies interest in CA.</title>
<headline>Bank Austria denies interest in CA.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Austria on Tuesday denied media reports that it was planning to submit a bid for its main rival, privatisation candidate Creditanstalt-Bankverein by the government's final December 16 deadline.</p>
<p>A Bank Austria spokesman said the bank had &quot;no interest&quot; in buying into Creditanstalt.</p>
<p>Austrian media, desperate to pinpoint Finance Minister Viktor Klima's second, secretive indicative bidder for Creditanstalt, have settled on Bank Austria as a possible contender.</p>
<p>A consortium round insurer EA-Generali has so far made the only public bid for Creditanstalt, which has been on the government's sell-off list since the autumn of 1990.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom 43-1-531 12 254</p>
